#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552598} :activity/id #uuid "31c60258-9499-522d-a1d7-bc4dbf27dc64" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050524 :topic/id #uuid "505d75ff-8395-5a7e-8e48-f2062c75044a" :topic/math-academy-id 2141} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552527 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552448 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35dd6086-4251-55ee-bf1d-0d4170f92806" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551794} {:answer/id #uuid "7377b049-86e3-553e-b830-866c1ab90043" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551940} {:answer/id #uuid "7964ac04-8e18-5c1f-9351-0d3d8a0643a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551952} {:answer/id #uuid "83b6967e-1866-5b1d-bec6-4239de727c29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551978} {:answer/id #uuid "84a1c1dc-9d6d-5817-a3a8-a8962b94ece3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551984}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551952} :answer-field/id #uuid "52c6f404-4a46-5339-9b41-fcaeb9813680" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552299}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "688ce6d7-73b6-5ba5-87a1-28b0bc9bdadb" :question/math-academy-id "q-161592" :question/problem "![](images/f2/f2f91e4ee1a90e1afb00d2f212e057235afe5c4e9089679da3af244c1d324676.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}12x\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](images/b7/b7e71e46310b065e2c03b4a0aebaa96268136c7f633eea6983612297e56361d1.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 1+y+z\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/14/145f0d494ffe24de84e3a289b3a7316d3f4933f193d734aed118609f7fb9f94f.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 1+y+z\\}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}12x\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1+y+z}12x\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1+y+z}12x\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1+y+z}12x\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[6{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=1+y+z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}6(1+y+z)^{2}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(6+6{y}^{2}+6{z}^{2}+12yz+12y+12z)\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(6+6{y}^{2}+6{z}^{2}+12yz+12y+12z)\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}(6+6{y}^{2}+6{z}^{2}+12yz+12y+12z)\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[6z+6{y}^{2}z+2{z}^{3}+6y{z}^{2}+12yz+6{z}^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(6+6{y}^{2}+2+6y+12y+6)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(6{y}^{2}+18y+14)\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(6{y}^{2}+18y+14)\\,dy & =[2{y}^{3}+9{y}^{2}+14y]_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =(2+9+14)-0 \\\\  & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "00fbf4c2-2801-5993-ad8e-f84d0f4127a2"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552568 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278560 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aa387c3-44ed-5bd4-9f84-186d277c7b83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275567} {:answer/id #uuid "0fbce1a0-73cf-5680-8b10-d475399b02ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275613} {:answer/id #uuid "8765e484-8aa6-597f-a01c-28e611f4203e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276698} {:answer/id #uuid "bd467838-92ab-5a7b-b7b4-f3f80d1d157c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277163} {:answer/id #uuid "c4b805e1-48ea-506e-b60f-f298e1409b71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277225}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277163} :answer-field/id #uuid "27dcffb3-d41f-5092-b14f-f7e45e7ff8ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277790}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4d010482-1691-5f93-8b77-314a6b05233e" :question/math-academy-id "q-161571" :question/problem "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2z}}\\frac{x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,y\\le z\\le y+1\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2z}}\\frac{x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{4}[{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{2z}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{4}(2z-0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{2}z\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{2}z\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{y}^{y+1}\\frac{1}{2}z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{4}[{z}^{2}]_{z=y}^{z=y+1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{4}((y+1)^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{4}(2y+1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[{y}^{2}+y]}_{y=1}^{y=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(9+3)-\\frac{1}{4}(1+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "76b13d88-abdf-5c32-ac62-13913da93605" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552583}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552577 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278559 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38384fb9-4559-5dfb-b210-72b9cc741634" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275973} {:answer/id #uuid "43967edf-f566-5b5c-8be1-4f953f652870" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276076} {:answer/id #uuid "7147d6ac-0197-5051-a9d9-d6fc981d89bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "68" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276497} {:answer/id #uuid "e808d2fe-b5fd-51ad-8ceb-875830565f95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277508} {:answer/id #uuid "f190aad5-a265-579f-bbd3-464e3c65ff79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277597}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277597} :answer-field/id #uuid "066e7a1a-27a5-5cdc-96a1-c8fdeb17fa35" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277739}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0286c07f-b1b2-5473-afd1-f9920e12c0a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-161570" :question/problem "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}4x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,0\\le z\\le y\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}4x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}2[{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2({(\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}})}^{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{y}2{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[2{y}^{2}z+\\frac{2}{3}{z}^{3}]}_{z=0}^{z=y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2{y}^{3}+\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{8}{3}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(81-0) \\\\  & =54\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "8bab914b-54f6-51bc-a2eb-35d5ba0ce55e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552568}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552583 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278564 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "085c1595-a112-5975-b0d5-4d9de18a8662" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275550} {:answer/id #uuid "682d6780-8947-5d0e-b0dc-7db62594be64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276408} {:answer/id #uuid "9e58c126-750e-5bf7-8442-99ef25280299" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276901} {:answer/id #uuid "9f096ac0-1861-594e-90f9-8e225ffdb6a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276905} {:answer/id #uuid "fc0432a2-2750-536b-b704-504d143f0258" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277688}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275550} :answer-field/id #uuid "81ca88ac-5791-5a5f-ab97-ee64c4045346" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277952}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "66331791-83b0-58ae-948f-5ef4e17dacab" :question/math-academy-id "q-161581" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}y\\,dV\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,0\\le x\\le y+z+2\\},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is a finite region in $yz$-plane enclosed between the $y$-axis, the $z$-axis and the line $z=2-y$ in the first quadrant." :question/worked-solution "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}y\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{y+z+2}y\\,dx]dA.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{y+z+2}y\\,dx]dA & ={∬}_{D}y[x]_{x=0}^{x=y+z+2}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}y(y+z+2)\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}+yz+2y\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now evaluate the double integral above over the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](images/b4/b473cc75dbbd6fa36ba43f6bbdec4a0133164e6fd8bc5f76ff86cec74714a256.png)\n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{y}^{2}+yz+2y\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-y}{y}^{2}+yz+2y\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2-y}{y}^{2}+yz+2y\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[({y}^{2}+2y)z+\\frac{1}{2}y{z}^{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=2-y}dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({y}^{2}+2y)(2-y)+\\frac{1}{2}y(2-y)^{2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(4y-{y}^{3})+\\frac{1}{2}y(4-4y+{y}^{2})\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{3}-2{y}^{2}+6y\\,dy \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{8}{y}^{4}-\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}+3{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =-2-\\frac{16}{3}+12 \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "93aaebfc-5a26-527f-82d4-f49bf1fd852a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552527}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552598 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552401 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0db88087-7cd2-5ed0-8f3f-ed5c64f026b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551700} {:answer/id #uuid "579006a3-9d2b-50bd-bf7d-e65f8b504a72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551874} {:answer/id #uuid "908aa92d-d371-5a1f-903d-19816c117bbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{y}^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552018} {:answer/id #uuid "cb549a3d-f2e1-5432-8a0b-ea396cd96379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{y}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552151} {:answer/id #uuid "ea286272-e0fc-510b-b716-553bbe28b58d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1-{y}^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552214}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552151} :answer-field/id #uuid "25ad75a8-02de-5c76-b6ba-6c420483aaa3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552274}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "01bff6b1-8c04-5993-b5c1-12639cb1fb77" :question/math-academy-id "q-161551" :question/problem "![](images/6e/6e5cb856069061be9b877753ce6c373ee9191547fce8750e9c2a8b073b99ceb0.png)\n\nGiven that $R$ is the type II region shown above, \n${∭}_{R}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}V=$" :question/worked-solution "For a type II region $R$ with projection $D$ onto the $yz$-plane, the triple integral of a continuous function $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe consider the region $R$ as a type II region enclosed between the back surface $x={u}_{1}(y,z)=1$ and the front surface $x={u}_{2}(y,z)=2.$\n\n![](images/e5/e5779dc92c875bef280425ed24a17cfb53f9f2a9736292a92ccdb988044237a6.png)\n\nSo, the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,1\\le x\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ as a type I *plane* region in the $yz$-plane with the upper curve\n\n$$\nz=1-{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\n![](images/00/00f2847a8e4c927a1c6631f4aef03c57b9d28f18341b268182501ada07225382.png)\n\nHence, $D=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 1-{y}^{2}\\}.$\n\nTherefore, we write the triple integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}V & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{y}^{2}}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{y}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z[x]_{x=1}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{y}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "bd18d575-4084-57e8-b00e-0672dad4d781" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552577}}] :activity/title "Triple Integrals Over Type II Regions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551648}]}
